These headers are for syntax checks only and are not part of any
build: they let the Mac compile src/zfsops.c with -DZR_FREEBSD and
-fsyntax-only, so that a wrong argument count or a dropped const is
caught here rather than on the box. The declarations in them are
copied verbatim from the FreeBSD source tree under
sys/contrib/openzfs (CDDL-1.0, OpenZFS), with the file each block
came from named above it; only the opaque stand-in typedefs and the
guards are ours. Nothing here is authoritative: the FreeBSD tree is,
and the box's own compiler is the last word.

    cc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wcast-qual -fsyntax-only \
        -DZR_FREEBSD -Itests/stub -Isrc src/zfsops.c

